        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c69bbf9c-00ac-5c6e-895a-1188011d4fa7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bhupen Hazarika, Ram Niwas Mirdha\n- Organizations: Sangeet Natak Akademi, Government of India\n- Awards: Padmashri, Sangeet Natak Akademi Award, Dada Saheb Phalke Award, Padmabhushan, Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship\n- Works: Daina (1984 film)\n- Concepts: The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama\n\nFacts:\n- In 1977, Bhupen Hazarika received the Padmashri award.\n- In 1984, Dr. Bhupen Hazarika composed the music for the film Daina.\n- In 1987, Bhupen Hazarika received the Sangeet Natak Akademi Award.\n- In 1992, the Government of India awarded Bhupen Hazarika the Dada Saheb Phalke Award, India's highest award in cinema.\n- In 2001, Bhupen Hazarika received the Padmabhushan award.\n- In 2008, Bhupen Hazarika received the Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship, the highest award of the Sangeet Natak Akademi.\n- Sangeet Natak Akademi is the national-level academy for performing arts set up by the Government of India.\n- Sangeet Natak Akademi is also known in English as The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama.\n- Ram Niwas Mirdha served as chairman of the Sangeet Natak Akademi until his death from multiple organ failure.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2c0612df-8978-5d06-a69a-ef00c98b0161",
        "text": "Page: Bhupen Hazarika. Sentence: Recipient of Sangeet Natak Akademi Award (1987), Padmashri (1977), and Padmabhushan (2001), Hazarika was awarded with Dada Saheb Phalke Award (1992), India's highest award in cinema, by the Government of India and Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship (2008), the highest award of the Sangeet Natak Akademi, India's The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama.\nPage: Sangeet Natak Akademi. Sentence: Sangeet Natak Akademi (Devanāgarī: \"संगीत नाटक अकादेमी\" or The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama in English) is the national level academy for performing arts set up by the Government of India.\nPage: Daina (1984 film). Sentence: The music for the film is composed by Dr. Bhupen Hazarika.\nPage: Ram Niwas Mirdha. Sentence: He served as chairman of the Sangeet Natak Akademi until his death from multiple organ failure.",
